  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "CAP-001",
      "kind": "confirmed_boundary",
      "summary": "The observed DeepSeek Worker runs retain100M model windows while their token allocations are166667/166666. The replacement GLM profile has its separate1M window. Lower request input allowances do not rewrite these capacities."
    },
    {
      "id": "CAP-002",
      "kind": "latent_feedback_label_defect_not_exercised_by_observed_continuity_workers",
      "references": [
        "worker_runtime.py:2449",
        "worker_runtime.py:2508"
      ],
      "summary": "With a review/worker capacity policy, cycle.current_request_allowance replaces remaining, but the prompt key remains remaining_cumulative_tokens. It can describe current-request allowance as cumulative balance. Original gates remain separate. Observed continuity capsules have neither capacity policy."
    },
    {
      "id": "CAP-003",
      "kind": "observed_diagnostic_gap",
      "references": [
        "worker_model_compaction.py:272",
        "context_service.py:886",
        "worker_runtime.py:2594"
      ],
      "summary": "invalid_compaction_handoff merges several response and source-bound checks. Rejection events omit compaction call_id, response hash, byte count, finish/tool metadata and fixed subreason. The failed response is not saved to worker_messages or an archive, so its concrete shape/category cannot be recovered."
    },
    {
      "id": "CAP-004",
      "kind": "diagnostic_timestamp_scope_gap",
      "references": [
        "worker_runtime.py:2459",
        "worker_runtime.py:2602"
      ],
      "summary": "request_token_allowance is calculated before a compaction call; cumulative_token_remaining is reread after the failed call has settled. The event can show allowance50223 vs later balance36826, or50052 vs40680. These are different accounting instants, not evidence of a request admitted beyond its budget."
    },
    {
      "id": "CAP-005",
      "kind": "safe_availability_limit_static_only",
      "references": [
        "model_compaction.py:187",
        "router.py:841",
        "model_call_budget.py:465"
      ],
      "summary": "Router and Router compactor size to model capacity without proactively selecting a smaller affordable complete prefix. A payload that fits the model may still be safely rejected at cumulative Gateway admission. This is not context-capacity mixing and is not established as an observed task failure here."
    },
    {
      "id": "CAP-006",
      "kind": "observability_limit",
      "summary": "Actual ModelRequest.context_limit is not durably snapshotted for every call. Frozen source, explicit driver cap, Registry/run records and context-rejection diagnostics bind the runtime capacity, but ledger reservations alone cannot prove every transmitted request field. Serialized UTF8-byte sizing is a conservative token upper bound, not tokenized capacity measurement."
    }
  ],
